One other point – we might just settle this so delay is good.&nbsp;​​​​Craig&nbsp;Shuttleworth+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7770&nbsp;847&nbsp;435From: Craig Shuttleworth Sent: 30 October 2025 17:52To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;craig@kastlesolicitors.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Holly Hampton &lt;hhampton@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Federica Lombardi &lt;flombardi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;craig@kastlesolicitors.com&gt;Subject: RE: Report&nbsp;Celine is on gardening leave; she will help answering questions but is not actively Involved in anything.&nbsp;My concerns re avoiding the TG issue are legion.&nbsp;He was Global Managing Partner and owner.He signed documents saying he was conducting the case.He did in fact conduct the case.The evidence of that is everywhere, and if they don’t have enough others will provide it.The firm must carry some responsibility for the past.We need to draw a distinction between the past and the present.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 October 2025 16:41To: Craig Shuttleworth &lt;craig@kastlesolicitors.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Holly Hampton &lt;hhampton@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Federica Lombardi &lt;flombardi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Report&nbsp;Also, what is Celine's status at the moment - is she on gardening leave? I would assume we can't say that she &quot;has direct responsibility for&quot;&nbsp;It's fine to not comment on TG's responsibilities but do we need to say something about the firm's own responsibilities?&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Craig Shuttleworth &lt;craig@kastlesolicitors.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Thursday, October 30, 2025 4:28 P