sultant point:&nbsp;There is no inherent regulatory bar on a solicitor at another firm being engaged to work as a consultant on a particular matter.&nbsp; From a conduct of litigation perspective, I don’t see any problem with this.&nbsp;There are of course a raft of issues that any such consultancy arrangement would need to address, e.g. how to deal with conflicts of interest, lines of supervision/responsibility, client consent, the terms of the consultancy engagement, and no doubt various other issues.&nbsp; There will always be questions that can be asked about these arrangements, but (a) I’m not sure that there would be any real justification for Slaughters probing into them, and (b) there is no reason why these points can’t be satisfactorily dealt with by a suitable consultancy agreement, such that it can work without any giving rise to any regulatory problems.&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Craig Shuttleworth &lt;craig@kastlesolicitors.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Thursday, October 30, 2025 3:49 PMTo:&nbsp;Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;; Holly Hampton &lt;hhampton@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Federica Lombardi &lt;flombardi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Report&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Can we fix a call early next week ?&nbsp;Craig Shuttleworth07770 847435&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Craig ShuttleworthSent:&nbsp;30 October 2025 14:37To:&nbsp;'Matthew Getz' &lt;Matthew.Getz@pal