&nbsp;
We will need to discuss further how the cross-collateralisation of the additional layers would coexist within the waterfall, particularly in relation to the cross-collateralisation of emissions proceeds
 in the 4th layer of the BHP ATE policy (as formalised in the Reimbursement Deed), which sets out payment of reimbursement out of 50% of PG net proceeds from Nox cases after taxes, insurers, counsel, and payments to funders, including Gramercy facilities.
&nbsp;
Economic Terms of the Top-Up
&nbsp;
