 breach of 1.4 of the code of conduct. This applies not only to correspondence to the Defendant firms, but also to clients and any external parties.&nbsp;This requires immediate attention, especially in respect of my position.&nbsp;&nbsp;SL have asked for a response by 4pm. Without wanting to force the hands of the board, I must be insistent that the below (or clarification of that nature) is sent before that deadline to clarify the position:&nbsp;&quot;Pogust Goodhead are considering your application and will respond in due course.&nbsp;&nbsp;As an immediate step, and to address 8(b)(iii) in your application, we confirm categorically that MR Burke does not have conduct of these Pan NOx Litigations. The inclusion of Mr Burke's details in the letter sent to the Defendants on 24 September which named Michael Burke as a &quot;contact&quot;, this was an oversight, and this does not indicate that Mr Burke has conduct of these Pan NOx Litigations on behalf of Pogust Goodhead and Pogust Goodhead's clients. For absolute clarity, Mr Burke does not have conduct of the Pan-NOx Litigations on behalf of Pogust Goodhead.&nbsp;&nbsp;Mr Burke currently has conduct of the Ford NOx Litigation, and the Volvo NOx Litigation, as part of the Pan NOx Litigations. The overall supervision of the Pan-NOx Litigations for Pogust Goodhead will be confirmed in due course as requested in your application.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We also take this opportunity to advise the Defendants, that Mr Burke has formally tendered his resignation with Pogust Goodhead, as of 15 September 2025, and he is currently working his notice period, the end date which is to be confirmed. Correspondence will be sent directly to the Defendants in those Litigations as soon as possible.&quot;&nbsp;This needs to be sent as soon as possible. I imagine this may be an opportune moment to advise on the other Case Leads and I am happy for this to be incorporated, but the clarity on my position needs to be dealt with immediately.&nbsp;&