Hi Both &nbsp;See below analysis of the topup in adverse costs cover that we have asked our brokers to arrange:&nbsp;&nbsp;Adverse Costs Exposure (to Jul 26)LOI in placeSurplus / (Shortfall)Topup requiredAs % LOIMercedes11,263,0098,454,172-2,808,8372,808,83733%Ford15,131,21111,105,133-4,026,0794,026,07936%RN25,493,36018,550,234-6,943,1266,943,12637%Citroen-Peugeot9,901,3528,115,744-1,785,6081,785,60822%BMW3,941,7425,000,0001,058,25800%FCA8,824,9858,205,964-619,021619,0218%JLR2,816,4272,821,4084,98100%Hyundai-Kia1,865,3021,677,429-187,873187,87311%VW2 Porsche6,983,8197,141,252157,43300%Vauxhall1,916,3942,000,00083,60600%Volvo1,681,3605,000,0003,318,64000%Mazda2,688,2812,685,173-3,1083,1080%Toyota3,442,2082,951,874-490,333490,33317%Ds’ Incurred Costs CMH1  (up to 13 June 2024) (Exc KBA) - Total95,949,45283,708,383-12,241,06916,863,98620%&nbsp;This would provide sufficient indemnity to cover the claimant’s cost exposure to 31 July 2026, as per the assumptions outlined in Anna’s email. &nbsp;The brokers have indicated that they are able to provide a quote for some of the required topup by the end of the week, exact amounts per manufacturer will be provided tomorrow. &nbsp;It is not clear on the timing or certainty of availability of the remainder of the topup as the brokers have to approach the open market. I expect to have an update on this position tomorrow also. &nbsp;Tom&nbsp;&nbsp;From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 22 October 2025 20:31To: T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.comCc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Hi Theo&nbsp;See below a break down of the additional cover that is being sought - this aligns with the approach Leigh Day is taking. I don't yet have pro rated cover per defendant: @Tom Crow&nbsp;is that something you could assist with please?&nbsp;60% of the Defendants incurred costs (including those from CMH1 and CMH2, the costs of cost budgeting from both CMH1 and CMH2, and the Non-Tranche 3 Quantum costs).100% of the Defendants Tranche 2 (£90.5 million) and First General approved future costs (£19.25 million)Defendants Tranche 3 approved future costs up to 31 July 2026, broken down as follows:100% of CMC, Selection of Sample Claimants, Individual Statements of Case, Disclosure, Witness Statements, and PTR71% of the Tranche 3 Co-Ordination Costs (12.5 out of 17.5 months)Trial Preparation: We had been considering seeking between 33% and 50%. However, Leigh Day is seeking 50%, and we consider a more conservative approach is appropriate in light of the scrutiny. If we go with 50% this would add c. £1.5 million LOI which we can accommodate in the budget. &nbsp;Defendants Second General approved future costs up to 31 July 2026, broken down as follows:44% of GLO Management CostsFortnightly Meetings to September 2026 at 67%T3 Expert Reports/2G ADR: Figures based on Claimant offers. 100% of £10.2m for expert reports, and 44% of £1.8m for ADR. Leigh Day have based their approach on agreed figures, with the following exceptions: &nbsp;where not agreed, Defendants counteroffer, and where no counteroffer, Claimants offer).&nbsp;BestAnna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent: Wednesday, October 22, 2025 8:08 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2 &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Anna&nbsp;&nbsp;Can you let me know how much further ate cover you are planning to get and what the total pro rated cover per defendant solicitors firm is anticipated to be? That makes &nbsp;a&nbsp;difference, I think, to whether we should say more. If we anticipate getting very close to eliminating the shortfalls, then I would be more in favour of saying so. If we are still going to be way off, it’s probably less good an idea.&nbsp;Thanks&nbsp;Theo &nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOSTheo&nbsp;Barclay​​​​BarristerDirect&nbsp;+442078222100&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;+447411&nbsp;731074&nbsp;Chambers&nbsp;+442078222000&nbsp;4&nbsp;New&nbsp;Square&nbsp;Chambers​Lincoln's&nbsp;Inn,&nbsp;London&nbsp;WC2A&nbsp;3RJFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;YouTube&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedIn​Discover&nbsp;our&nbsp;Events&nbsp;Privilege and Confidentiality Notice:This email is private as between the sender and the intended recipient. The information contained in this message and any file that may be attached to it are confidential between those parties and may be privileged. Any other party who receives it in error is not permitted to read, use, copy, discuss or pass on the information contained in either the message or its attachments, nor are they entitled to take any action in reliance on the contents. Therefore, if you are not the intended recipient you are kindly requested to contact me immediately by telephone on the numbers given above.Members of 4 New Square Chambers are regulated by the Bar Standards Board.NOTE TO SOLICITORS: ALL PAPERS RECEIVED FOR MEMBERS OF CHAMBERS WILL BE SENT FOR SECURE SHREDDING&nbsp;UPON COMPLETION OF WORK&nbsp;UNLESS YOU SPECIFICALLY REQUEST THEIR RETURN.From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Wednesday, October 22, 2025 8:02:14 PMTo: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: Benjamin Williams KC &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2 &nbsp;EXTERNAL EMAILTheo&nbsp;Please find attached draft response - grateful if you could consider and comment.&nbsp;&nbsp;Note 2 specific queries:&nbsp;1. Re confirming we are seeking additional cover. This is in hand but we don't yet have timings etc. See my comment at para 3.2. See the comment at para 4(c)(ii) re a case citation - please would you confirm.&nbsp;We are looking to send the letter tomorrow.&nbsp;BestAnna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Tuesday, October 21, 2025 2:20 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; T.Barclay@4newsquare.com &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2 &nbsp;Theo, Simon&nbsp;Further to Anna’s email please see attached: PG letter dated 10 October re ATE &amp; funding as sent (with appendices)PG’s holding response dated 20 October to the Defendants in response to their letters of 17 OctoberLetter from Gramercy (BSF) dated 20 October in response to the Defendants letters of 17 OctoberLetter from Hogan Lovells dated 20 October in response to PG’s letter of 10 October &nbsp;Kind RegardsJess &nbsp;Jessica Fechner (she/her)Associate (England &amp; Wales qualified) Amsterdam &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 21 October 2025 13:57To: T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Theo, Simon&nbsp;Thank you both for your input in relation to 10 October letter. Simon - I understand you are in a heavy hearing at the moment - best of luck.&nbsp;&nbsp;Theo - we received several letters from Ds about the ATE and funding info disclosure (all within 1.5hrs on Friday evening). Besides a holding response, we are yet to respond substantively. There is a draft response in the works, which we will share today/tomorrow. In the meantime, I wanted to bring this to your attention - not least because any application for disclosure etc will be made 24th&nbsp;October. I've attached the relevant letters and the team will share the draft response once ready. Grateful for you input at such time. In addition, as will have been obvious to you both, we are in the process of sorting additional ATE and the team can update with details/timings.&nbsp;@Jessica Fechner&nbsp;please could you share (as sent) 10 October letter, holding response and check I have not omitted any correspondence on this topic.&nbsp;BestAnna&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Thursday, October 9, 2025 10:09 PMTo:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Dear Tom,&nbsp;Please see attached a draft of the letter with my suggested amendments and comments.&nbsp;The most important point here is to make sure that what is said about PG’s funding agreements is accurate and not misleading by omission, because anything that isn’t quite right (or a relevant funding arrangement not included) will doubtless be seized on down the line.&nbsp;On the ATE assumptions, my views are as follows (and I know these are shared by Simon):&nbsp;We think that future costs for ADR and Experts should be included in the relevant expenditure calculations. Despite not having been assessed by the court yet, those costs would be incurred within the relevant period and therefore will be taken into account when assessing of sufficiency of cover. It would be reasonable at this stage to take the Claimants’ offers against those phases as the starting point for what we say is required, but we must recognise that leaving those phases out altogether isn’t going to be defensible before the court. So if para 9a and 9b are to go into the letter (and I can see they may be needed for now if the position on sufficiency of cover is to be maintained) we need to accept internally that there will need to be movement on that point (and additional cover) if the position on ATE sufficiency is to be maintained before the court.&nbsp;Similarly, we don’t think there is a strong case for downgrading the % of incurred costs by 10%. Again, if this is to go into the letter we ought to treat it internally as a holding position while you look to increase cover.&nbsp;We agree that it is not sensible to disclose in the letter that you are looking to increase cover. Most importantly, that essentially amounts to a concession that what you have is insufficient - and additionally, as you point out, you may not be able to secure further cover and we don’t want to box ourselves in.&nbsp;I hope that helps. I am around tomorrow morning if needed until around 1pm.&nbsp;Many thanks,&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Barclay​​​​BarristerDirect&nbsp;+442078222100&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;+447411&nbsp;731074&nbsp;Chambers&nbsp;+442078222000&nbsp;4&nbsp;New&nbsp;Square&nbsp;Chambers​Lincoln's&nbsp;Inn,&nbsp;London&nbsp;WC2A&nbsp;3RJFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;YouTube | LinkedIn​Discover&nbsp;our Events&nbsp;Privilege and Confidentiality Notice:This email is private as between the sender and the intended recipient. The information contained in this message and any file that may be attached to it are confidential between those parties and may be privileged. Any other party who receives it in error is not permitted to read, use, copy, discuss or pass on the information contained in either the message or its attachments, nor are they entitled to take any action in reliance on the contents. Therefore, if you are not the intended recipient you are kindly requested to contact me immediately by telephone on the numbers given above.Members of 4 New Square Chambers are regulated by the Bar Standards Board.NOTE TO SOLICITORS: ALL PAPERS RECEIVED FOR MEMBERS OF CHAMBERS WILL BE SENT FOR SECURE SHREDDING&nbsp;UPON COMPLETION OF WORK&nbsp;UNLESS YOU SPECIFICALLY REQUEST THEIR RETURN.From: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Thursday, 9 October 2025 at 19:39To: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;, Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: Benjamin Williams KC &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2EXTERNAL EMAIL+Simon Teasdale&nbsp;Hi Theo&nbsp;Thank you for your time earlier and agreeing to provide comment on this letter. If you could please provide your thoughts on the entirety of the letter it would be greatly appreciated.&nbsp;I attach the latest draft of the letter which amends the funding disclosure section to align it more closely with witness statements recently submitted to court.&nbsp;We discussed with Simon yesterday some of the assumptions and caveats we are making in our calculations of projected expenditure to July 2026 (when we expect to receive a decision on PDD). It would be helpful to confirm your /Simon’s views on us making these statements in the letter:&nbsp;Para 9a confirms that costs for the ADR/Settlement phase has not been included in the expenditure calculations as they have not yet been approvedPara 9b confirms that costs for the Expert Reports phase have not been included in the expenditure calculations as they have not yet been approvedPara 13 confirms we are reducing the percentages applied to claimed incurred costs and costs of cost budgeting, the rationale being provided in para 16 (i.e. they are disproportionate and distort the sufficiency analysis)&nbsp;As discussed, these assumptions around calculating expenditure to the decision on PDD, which we believe are reasonable, help to demonstrate that we currently have sufficient cover. Once these points are factored into the calculations it is likely that the shortfall in ATE cover to July 26 will increase.&nbsp;Internally, we are working toward increasing our level of cover, however we know that there are issues around capacity in the market and there may be challenges in securing topups to our cover. We therefore do not feel that it is appropriate to disclose that we are looking to increase capacity in this letter.&nbsp;Please let us know your thoughts&nbsp;RegardsTom&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at 53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website. For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;09 October 2025 16:56To:&nbsp;T.Barclay@