Neil,Please find below:&nbsp;The firm’s most recent funding, to pay all expected outgoings until the conclusion of the PDD Trial hearing in December, is comprised of the following provided by funds managed by Gramercy Fund Management LLC (“Gramercy”): (a) a $65 million facility made available on 14 August 2025 (“August Tranche”) under a corporate debt facility of $65million (“Gramercy 3”), and (b) a $30 million facility made available on 19 September 2025 (“September Tranche”) under a corporate debt facility of $582.5 million (“Gramercy 1” and Gramercy 3, collectively, the “Funding”). The August Tranche is available for firm overhead and not on specific NOx Group Litigations fees whilst the September Tranche can contractually be used only for the NOx Group Litigations. The Funding operates as corporate debt facilities whereby Pogust Goodhead makes regular drawdowns in line with requirements.&nbsp;&nbsp;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 10 October 2025 10:39To: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;We are happy on the changes with the only additional changes as marked below please would @Carolina Koschdoski de Souza confirm that is correct as marked below.&nbsp;Many thanks,&nbsp;Neil&nbsp;&nbsp;Neil&nbsp;Pigott​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1005|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;75&nbsp;5741&nbsp;2828E:&nbsp;&nbsp;neil.pigott@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 10 October 2025 14:29To: Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Hi Neil &nbsp;We need to make some final tweaks to %’s to reflect the revised calculations as discussed over the last few days. &nbsp;We also need to amend the headings on the table (which currently read “LOI Top Up Required”)&nbsp;If you can confirm once you are happy with the changes I can apply these final adjustments&nbsp;Tom&nbsp;​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.